    {
      "id": "50aca4c2d23d4ff5b7f624afc9fabadfd615d476",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": true,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2156526692,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "As said previously MBIM is a standard specifically designed for cellular modem, not a UICC reader protocol. That's why I prhposely chose the gsm_sim dissector to be the default one. I'm fine adding a fallback to the iso7816 one from the gsm_qil depending on the CLA byte as I think it makes sense, with a preference on by default.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6722527,
            "username": "pquantin",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Pascal Quantin",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/9bf49edc6acae0eca821eb90309381794fb4fbea4f3fb7c2378428862ddbb430?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/pquantin"
          },
          "created_at": "2024-10-13T15:25:15.839Z",
          "updated_at": "2024-10-13T20:07:19.825Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 333592900,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": true,
          "resolved_by": {
            "id": 6722527,
            "username": "pquantin",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Pascal Quantin",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/9bf49edc6acae0eca821eb90309381794fb4fbea4f3fb7c2378428862ddbb430?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/pquantin"
          },
          "resolved_at": "2024-10-13T20:07:19.825Z",
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 17644,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 2156538796,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "If \"proprietary\" 0x8 CLA is specific to all (e)SIM cards, I'm not sure if we need such CLA parsing for MBIM case at all (which as we learned should be `gsm_sim` by default).\n\nBut for CCID USB reader case, we now know ISO-7816 dissector is better default (if we still need the default there), and considering we can insert in the reader SIM cards, too - we need proper CLA parsing in the ISO-7816 dissector (if that needs to be done in dissector), with fallback to gsm_sim.\n\nOr maybe do that CLA parsing in the upper \"CCID USB\" layer then, I don't know.\n\nThoughts?",
          "author": {
            "id": 1199718,
            "username": "bam80",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Andrey",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/7ab86baac98545d1d9105f4a32741596139828706fc4fc7e7905ac689774f54b?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/bam80"
          },
          "created_at": "2024-10-13T16:40:54.695Z",
          "updated_at": "2024-10-13T20:07:19.825Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 333592900,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": true,
          "resolved_by": {
            "id": 6722527,
            "username": "pquantin",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Pascal Quantin",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/9bf49edc6acae0eca821eb90309381794fb4fbea4f3fb7c2378428862ddbb430?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/pquantin"
          },
          "resolved_at": "2024-10-13T20:07:19.825Z",
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 17644,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 2156543497,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Sorry but I do not see why this discussion happens in a MBIM dissector patch: it has nothing to do with a USB CCID reader. And as already stated in the context of MBIM dissector, I do not think parsing the opaque UICC payload in USB dissector to identify the sub dissector to be called makes sense (that's not what we usually do).\nIf the ISO7816 specification (that I do not have) does not specify that the CLA byte MSB bit set to 1 means the proprietary 3GPP/ETSI implementation then you should not have this test done on its dissector. Having it the other way around makes sense as it is explicitly specified. Anyway any further discussion should be done in its own enhancement request.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6722527,
            "username": "pquantin",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Pascal Quantin",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/9bf49edc6acae0eca821eb90309381794fb4fbea4f3fb7c2378428862ddbb430?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/pquantin"
          },
          "created_at": "2024-10-13T17:14:01.652Z",
          "updated_at": "2024-10-13T20:07:19.825Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 333592900,
